<% content_for :title, "Terms of service" %>
<% content_for :description, "The terms on which HardPoint provides point of sale and stock control to hardware stores as a service: the trial, payment, read-only mode, your data, what we promise and what we don't." %>
<%# Plain-language terms, written to match how HardPoint actually works. Have a Kenyan lawyer review them before launch (docs/LAUNCH.md). %>

<article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16">
  <h1 class="text-4xl font-semibold">Terms of service</h1>
  <p class="mt-3 text-gray-600">The agreement between your shop and <%= @company[:name] %> ("HardPoint", "we") when you use HardPoint. Last changed <%= l(Date.new(2026, 11, 8), format: :long) %>.</p>

  <% [
    [ "The service", "HardPoint is point of sale and stock control for hardware stores, provided over the internet at your shop's own web address. We run it, keep it up to date and back it up; you use it from your own computers, tablets and phones. Your use of M-Pesa, Airtel Money, KRA eTIMS, text messages, card payments and WhatsApp through HardPoint is also subject to those providers' own terms." ],
    [ "Your account", "Whoever opens a shop on HardPoint must be entitled to act for that business. The owner is responsible for the people they add as staff, for keeping passwords, PINs and two-factor codes to the person they belong to, and for signing out devices the shop no longer uses. Tell us at once if you think an account has been misused." ],
    [ "The free trial", "Every new shop gets #{Plan::TRIAL.inspect} free with no card needed. At the end of the trial we invoice the plan you chose; if it isn't paid, the shop becomes read-only (see Payment). Nothing is deleted when a trial ends." ],
    [ "Payment", "Plans are priced per shop per month in Kenyan shillings, as on the pricing page, with monthly or yearly billing. We email each invoice and remind you before it's due. An invoice unpaid #{Plan::GRACE.inspect} after its date makes the shop read-only: you and your staff can still sign in, look things up and export your data, but can't sell or change anything until it's paid, after which everything works again at once. Setup visits, training and till kits are quoted and invoiced separately. Prices can change with 30 days' notice by email; a price change never applies to a period you've already paid for." ],
    [ "Changing plan and cancelling", "You can change plan, add or remove tills and branches, and switch between monthly and yearly billing from the Billing page at any time. You can close your shop at any time from Settings; you aren't charged after the period you've paid for, and yearly payments aren't refunded for the months left." ],
    [ "Your data", "Everything your shop enters or generates in HardPoint belongs to your shop. We process it only to provide the service, under the data processing terms, and never sell it or use it to advertise. You can export all of it as spreadsheets at any time, including while the shop is read-only. When you close the shop we delete its data 30 days later, except the invoices HardPoint issued to you, which tax law makes us keep." ],
    [ "What we promise", "We aim to keep HardPoint available all day, every day, and we commit to the uptime and support response times in the service level agreement for the Business and Enterprise plans. The till keeps selling when your internet is down and sends the sales when it's back. We back up every shop every hour and keep the backups encrypted off-site; you can also make and download your own backups from Settings." ],
    [ "What we don't promise", "HardPoint is provided as described, and we can't promise it will suit every purpose or never have faults. We aren't responsible for the services of Safaricom, Airtel, KRA, your bank, your internet provider or your hardware, for losses caused by wrong information entered into HardPoint, or for indirect losses such as lost profit. Our total liability to your shop for anything arising from the service in any twelve months is limited to the fees your shop paid us in those twelve months. Nothing in these terms limits liability that the law doesn't allow to be limited." ],
    [ "Acceptable use", "Use HardPoint for your own business only. Don't try to reach another shop's data, probe or overload the service, send unlawful or unsolicited messages through it, or resell it without an agreement with us. The API and webhooks come with their own limits, documented at /developers. We may suspend a shop that puts the service or other shops at risk, telling you why." ],
    [ "Changes to these terms", "When we change these terms we email every shop's owners at least 30 days before the change takes effect, and note the date at the top of this page. If you don't agree with a change, you can close your shop before it applies." ],
    [ "Law and disputes", "These terms are governed by the laws of Kenya. If something goes wrong, tell us first at #{Rails.configuration.x.support[:email]} and we'll try to put it right; failing that, the courts of Kenya have jurisdiction." ],
    [ "Who we are", "#{@company[:name]}, #{@company[:address]}#{", KRA PIN #{@company[:tax_pin]}" if @company[:tax_pin].present?}. Billing questions: #{@company[:email]}. Support: #{Rails.configuration.x.support[:email]}." ]
  ].each do |heading, body| %>
    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-bold"><%= heading %></h2>
    <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-gray-700"><%= body %></p>
  <% end %>

  <p class="mt-10 text-sm text-gray-600">See also: <%= link_to "data processing terms", data_processing_path, class: "link" %> · <%= link_to "privacy and your data", privacy_path, class: "link" %> · <%= link_to "service level agreement", sla_path, class: "link" %>.</p>
</article>
